course: dictionary
lesson: 14481
title: Words about family
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Paternal is a describing word. It means like a father, or to do with being a father. It can also mean related through your father.
explain: «My paternal grandmother lives in Leeds.» Her family link runs through your dad, so she is your father's mother. Look for the clue: the word grandmother tells you whose side she is on.
explain: «The kind teacher kept a paternal eye on every child.» A paternal teacher cares for others the way a father would: gently and protectively. Ask yourself, what would a caring father do? That is the meaning.
explain: Family trees use this word. Relatives on your father's side are paternal, and relatives on your mother's side are maternal. If you know one word, you can work out the other.
fact: Paternal means like a father, or related through your father.
fact: «Paternal» comes from the Latin word for father, pater.
fact: «Maternal» is the matching word for your mother's side of the family.
fact: «My paternal grandad» means your dad's dad.
fact: Male seahorses show paternal care: they carry the eggs in a pouch until the babies hatch.
exercise: «My paternal grandfather taught me to fish.» Whose father is he? | Your best friend's father | *Your dad's father | Your mum's father | Your teacher's father
exercise: «The male seahorse carried the eggs in its pouch.» What kind of care is this? | *Fatherly care, looking after the young | Care for the house | Teaching others to swim
exercise: Which word means related through your father? | Cheerful | Central | *Paternal | Maternal
test: «Her paternal uncle taught her to ride a bike.» What does paternal tell us? | Her uncle is a famous cyclist | Her uncle lives far away | *Her uncle is on her father's side of the family | Her uncle is on her mother's side
test: «The kind coach looked after the team like a paternal figure.» What does paternal figure mean? | *A caring person who protects others like a father would | A player who scores the most goals | A person who sells cars | A person who is always late
exam: Which side of a family tree are your maternal relatives on? | The top of the tree | The roots | Your father's side | *Your mother's side
